{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-99867",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we convert the given mixed number to an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n5\\,\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{(5\\times 3)+1}{3}=\\frac{16}{3}\n$$\n\nTo find the reciprocal of a fraction, we switch the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{16}{3}\\,\\to \\,\\frac{3}{16}\n$$\n\nSo the reciprocal of $\\frac{16}{3}$ is $\\frac{3}{16}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
